        <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl lg:text-4xl text-ink leading-tight mb-5">What is an Anxiety Disorder? Symptoms, Causes and Treatment</h1>
        <p class="text-ink-muted text-lg leading-relaxed">Anxiety is a part of life. But when it reaches a level that disrupts daily functioning, we can speak of an "anxiety disorder."</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-12 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <div class="prose-custom space-y-8">

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">The difference between anxiety and an anxiety disorder</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Nervousness before an exam, excitement before an important presentation, or fear when facing a dangerous situation — these are all normal, healthy forms of anxiety. This kind of anxiety motivates and protects us.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">An anxiety disorder is different: it is a chronic state of anxiety that arises without a real threat, or with an intensity far disproportionate to any actual threat, and that negatively affects daily life, relationships, and work or academic performance.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-primary/5 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-primary/15">
            <p class="text-sm text-ink font-medium mb-2">Awareness: How common is it?</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Approximately 284 million people worldwide live with an anxiety disorder — making anxiety the most prevalent mental health condition globally. (WHO, 2019)</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Types of anxiety disorder</h2>
            <div class="space-y-4">
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Generalised Anxiety Disorder (GAD)</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Excessive, uncontrollable worry across multiple areas lasting at least 6 months. Persistent concern about work, health, family, finances and similar topics.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Panic Disorder</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Sudden, intense fear episodes (panic attacks) characterised by palpitations, shortness of breath and fear of dying. Consists of recurring panic attacks.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Social Anxiety Disorder</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Fear of being judged, humiliated or embarrassed in social situations. Can lead to avoidance of social interactions and isolation.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Specific Phobias</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Disproportionate fear of specific objects or situations (heights, enclosed spaces, flying, spiders, etc.).</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Symptoms of anxiety disorder</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Symptoms can be grouped as emotional, cognitive and physical:</p>
            <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink mb-2">Emotional</p>
                <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1">
                  <li>• Persistent sense of dread</li>
                  <li>• Irritability and tension</li>
                  <li>• Fear of losing control</li>
                  <li>• Panic and terror</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink mb-2">Cognitive</p>
                <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1">
                  <li>• Difficulty concentrating</li>
                  <li>• Catastrophic thinking</li>
                  <li>• Indecisiveness</li>
                  <li>• Mind going "blank"</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink mb-2">Physical</p>
                <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1">
                  <li>• Palpitations, sweating</li>
                  <li>• Muscle tension</li>
                  <li>• Sleep problems</li>
                  <li>• Shortness of breath</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Treatment options</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Anxiety disorders are largely manageable with appropriate treatment. The main evidence-based approaches are:</p>
            <ul class="space-y-3">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Cognitive Behavioural Therapy (CBT)</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Focuses on recognising and changing the thought patterns that fuel anxiety. CBT has the strongest evidence base for anxiety disorders.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">EMDR</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Particularly effective for anxiety rooted in traumatic experiences.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Mindfulness-Based Approaches</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Breaks the anxiety cycle by learning to stay present in the moment.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-accent/5 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-accent/15">
            <p class="text-sm text-ink font-medium mb-2">When should you seek help?</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">If your anxiety is negatively affecting your work, relationships or daily functioning; if you have developed avoidance behaviours; or if you are experiencing sleep difficulties, it is advisable to speak to a professional.</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
